{"title":"1995 USAMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Alternate_Solution_(using_infinite_descent):\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Alternate Solution (using infinite descent):</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A calculator is broken so that the only keys that still work are the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/5/df52614a703f138f2273f30bb4954527ea3443b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, \\sin, \\; \\cos,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/9/ad9c561e76fb0d4f51d6e5e32c59ba4ec9c7e480.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan, \\; \\sin^{-1}, \\; \\cos^{-1}, \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd881c6b23858817681c2298c4c0f4c127e1e36f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, \\tan^{-1} \\,$\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" /> buttons.  The display initially shows 0. Given any positive rational number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/d/52de567b2fb907d7c3c52c250babad1ad4be5a22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, q, \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"11\" /> show that pressing some finite sequence of buttons will yield <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/7/b27d23e74c5dc135a9d69a0bc75edc98330ac011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\, q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" />.   Assume that the calculator does real number calculations with infinite precision.  All functions are in terms of radians.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will prove the following, stronger statement&#160;:  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime nonnegative integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/4/0247db3d702b5ce6be98f50771750a2723cddcea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, then the some finite sequence of buttons will yield <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/9154d0384033b6999ebdd12b4a55f342a456af06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{m/n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>To prove this statement, we induct strongly on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.  For our base case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/b/0bb3c3fc06952a2100f52121a8c5b403e14e575f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e275495e7e44d279fb3e5051b3a63115e79ead5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0ec2a4d556e9931baf61e1a076fb2cc833362e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{m/n} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"86\" height=\"32\" />, which is initially shown on the screen.  For the inductive step, we consider separately the cases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e275495e7e44d279fb3e5051b3a63115e79ead5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/8/d68b135073f700e45b55cd52b266d4bde12b0b31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;m\\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/c/9ecaf6f3eb60ec9df775d1f38929084fa9f0a2a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&lt;m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e275495e7e44d279fb3e5051b3a63115e79ead5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, and we have the base case.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/34963e7b7de6fd89b0c1f28cdec3bc4dd27ae8ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt; m \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />, then by inductive hypothesis, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/5/1b5bf1615ae4df39859082f8fd989f339de8087c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(n-m)/m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"106\" height=\"32\" /> can be obtained in finitely many steps; then so can\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/3/583351bb4f2162c99eb147802a903afc99d78df9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos \\tan^{-1} \\sqrt{(n-m)/m} = \\sqrt{m/n} .\\]\" width=\"261\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/c/9ecaf6f3eb60ec9df775d1f38929084fa9f0a2a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&lt;m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" />, then by the previous case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/9699d7e09cf0cb23e6acf87bf1ec768c34d520a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{n/m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"32\" /> can be obtained in finitely many steps.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/5/d05204c33e0d568357f48527cb71e13cfd1649b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\tan^{-1} \\sqrt{n/m} = \\sin \\tan^{-1} \\sqrt{m/n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"278\" height=\"32\" />, it follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75dce2211102fa0667cfb8e936d57f22cb6a0118.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan \\sin^{-1} \\cos \\tan^{-1} \\sqrt{n/m} = \\sqrt{m/n}\\]\" width=\"279\" height=\"32\" />\ncan be obtained in finitely many steps.  Thus the induction is complete.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Alternate_Solution_.28using_infinite_descent.29:\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alternate_Solution_(using_infinite_descent):\">Alternate Solution (using infinite descent):</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Alternate Solution (using infinite descent):\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This solution is similar to the above solution. We can invert a number with<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75dce2211102fa0667cfb8e936d57f22cb6a0118.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan \\sin^{-1} \\cos \\tan^{-1} \\sqrt{n/m} = \\sqrt{m/n}\\]\" width=\"279\" height=\"32\" /> and we can get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/e/16e4fb8107bf4daa868b24db6c0779b6beee3171.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan \\sin^{-1} \\cos \\tan^{-1}\\cos\\tan^{-1}\\sqrt{x} = \\sqrt{x + 1}.\\]\" width=\"331\" height=\"19\" />\nThen we do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/4805dddb4e6911989af8be91da334b5ba2054757.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27ce10a00966cc536c960489f12262253eb524d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> in reverse, trying to get 1. Subtracting one inside the radical for a fraction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/9154d0384033b6999ebdd12b4a55f342a456af06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{m/n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"32\" /> will eventually result in a fraction less than or equal to 1. Taking the reciprocal of this will result in a fraction greater than or equal to 1, and we can keep subtracting one inside the radical.\n</p><p>We do this repeatedly, and this should eventually result in 1 in a finite number of steps. This is because each time we do this, m+n is smaller. This is true even if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/9154d0384033b6999ebdd12b4a55f342a456af06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{m/n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"32\" /> can be simplified, as simplifying will only result in a smaller value. The smallest possible value of the fraction is 1/1, so this will be achieved after finite steps.\n</p><p>Finally, we know that 1 is achievable as cos(0) = 1.\n</p><p>~Unum\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO\" title=\"1995 USAMO\">1995 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1995 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1995\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1995 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1995 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1995 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1995 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1995 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1995 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/viewtopic.php?p=136808#136808\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016194219\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.065 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 217/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1617/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6029/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.192      1 -total\n 37.66%    6.475      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 32.63%    5.610      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 28.17%    4.843      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6389:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016194219 and revision id 120581. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}